From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Attard <sam@electronjs.org>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 02:44:34 +0000
Subject: build: allow resource allowlist generation for Linux

The resource allowlist machinery (grit --allowlist-support plus
tools/resources/generate_resource_allowlist.py) works on desktop Linux via
the same linker-input scanning path Android uses, but the assert in
gcc_toolchain.gni only permits android and win. Electron uses the allowlist
on Linux to repack its locale .pak files with only the strings its binary
references. (On macOS Electron reads the markers back from the linked
framework's symbol table and needs no toolchain change.)

Upstreamed at https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8360559.

diff --git a/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni b/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni
index ac7a5b84e93fd0bdf9eed224b2dd391621259636..68a744afb698cb4b62ff2830eac177f3460b48a9 100644
--- a/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni
+++ b/build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@ if (enable_resource_allowlist_generation) {
       !is_component_build,
       "enable_resource_allowlist_generation=true requires is_component_build=false")
   assert(
-      target_os == "android" || target_os == "win",
+      target_os == "android" || target_os == "win" || target_os == "linux",
       "enable_resource_allowlist_generation=true does not work for target_os=$target_os")
 }
 
